WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.130
Move to Frederic Church's
Twilight in the Wilderness, 1860.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.900
Nobody appears at all,
just glowing sky, brooding trees,

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.790
and water catching fire in the sunset.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.030
Church was famous
for staging his big canvases as events.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.690
His Heart of the Andes, the year before,

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.370
was shown alone in a darkened room
with curtains and gaslight,

7
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.450
and visitors paid admission to see it,
as if entering a temple.

8
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.250
The wilderness becomes spectacle:
sublime, gorgeous, unclaimed.
